From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 11:00:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] patch 0235 -- Campaign 2 AdLib: OPL2 backend + PIT-pump
 boot mode

The native-AdLib music path itself (Phase 1, explicit selection only).

WHY DOS needs this: lets a no-Sound-Blaster OPL card (incl. PicoGUS in
/mode adlib, which emulates OPL2 only) play Cave Story music natively on
the OPL chip. Today such a box can't even boot: SDL_Init(SDL_INIT_AUDIO)
fails with no SB and the engine exits.

- MidiBackendOpl2 (NEW class, lead decision (a) -- isolated from the
  shipped MidiBackendOpl3): 9-voice single-bank allocator on the OPL
  primary bank. Reuses the bank-agnostic SDL transport helpers
  (VoiceWritePatch/NoteOn/NoteOff) for voice 0-8 verbatim; OPL2-specific
  Detect/InitChip/Shutdown via SDL/0110. Loads the SAME data/opl3bank.dat
  DMXOPL GM bank (panning nibble no-ops on OPL2); honors patch[11]
  transpose (mirrors 0232). DPMI-locks under SDL_DOSMidiIsrAnyActive().

- main.cpp: AUDIO_BACKEND=adlib = THIRD boot mode -- omit SDL_INIT_AUDIO
  (no SB device to open) but KEEP SoundManager::init() (unlike AUDIO_OFF).
  Register an atexit SDL_DOSOplTimerPumpStop (PIT-ch0 restore safety).

- SoundManager::init: AdLib path skips the SB16 + SDL_mixer bring-up
  (MIX_Init / MIX_CreateMixerDevice), installs MidiBackendOpl2, registers
  the MIDI tick, then starts the PIT/IRQ-0 OPL pump as the clock (register
  BEFORE start so PumpStart snapshots the callback). hz from
  SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_OPL_TIMER_HZ (default 120, clamped [19,1000]).
  shutdown(): stop the pump FIRST (no IRQ into a torn-down backend; PIT
  restored), and skip MIX_Quit on the AdLib path (MIX_Init never ran).

MUSIC ONLY (lead-confirmed hard limit): a DAC-less AdLib card has no DMA,
so Pixtone PCM SFX cannot play; _mixer stays null and the SFX path no-ops.

Design: docs/internal/ADLIB-NATIVE-DESIGN.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
